## Delivered boundary

Bounded SDF/CIF/PDBx structure editing, identity/cell/sequence views and source-preserving import/export without physical execution.

## Ownership and possible overlap

Molecular structural profile, codec and native point/bond/sequence tools.

Independent ready packages may proceed together only after file/service ownership is reserved. Use separate leaf modules or isolated checkouts; shared migrations, command schemas, source/selection types, renderer lifetimes, runtime scheduling and performance sessions have one owner at a time. If actual code inspection finds an unproved shared boundary, add a dependency or serialize that work before coding. No promised worker count follows from the graph.

## Ordered work

Follow this package's task order. Original identifiers remain traceable; a reference to another former stage means its needed published contract, not an implicit global sequence. All native interaction, backend/persistence, authority, correctness and applicable resource obligations remain included.

### Task 12.T01

- [ ] **12.T01.** Implement finite-molecule, periodic-site and bounded protein profiles with compact stable IDs, species/isotope/charge fields, bonds/conformers, lattice/symmetry/occupancy and sequence/chain/residue/site mapping as applicable. Add declared SDF/CIF/PDBx-mmCIF subsets with source/license metadata and loss/unsupported reports.

### Task 12.T02

- [ ] **12.T02.** Add native point/bond/site/cell and sequence/structure selection/edit controls through I1–I5, numeric tools, supercell preview, validation diagnostics, undo and export. Keep display magnification, periodic images, physical amount and actual computational sample/population distinct.

### Task 12.T03

- [ ] **12.T03.** Open/save the protein specimen as its own root with no material/macro/Earth parent. Use the same native inspector/artifact contracts for structure metadata and authored state. Preserve protocol/observable extension points in the requirements; implementation of new measurement experiments/protocol execution and result comparisons waits for deferred [stage 17](../contracts/Laboratory-and-adoption-contracts.lingua).

### Task 12.T04

- [ ] **12.T04.** Test atom/bond/residue reorder, supported mirrored/stereochemical cases, missing/alternate sites, partial occupancies, nonorthogonal cells, duplicate symmetry expansion, invalid cells and stale structural/display jobs. Unsupported sequence-to-structure reconstruction remains an explicit draft/diagnostic. Do not compute density, energy, folding or force-field coverage as an implicit structural edit.

